the police were called to Nancy Pelosi's  San Francisco home just before 2 30 in  the morning she was away in Washington  and so it was her 82 year old husband  Paul who confronted the intruder  David de Pepe had entered through this  back door breaking the glass with a  hammer before hitting Mr Pelosi with it  he then tried to tie him up  when the police arrived both men were in  a struggle de Pepe telling them we're  waiting for Nancy  our officers immediately tackled the  suspect disarmed him took him into  custody requested emergency backup and  rendered Medical Aid  Mr Pelosi had been hit in the head with  the hammer multiple times he spent much  of the day in surgery  Nancy Pelosi is the third most senior  politician in America second in line to  the presidency she's among the most  prominent of Democratic party figures  and a key supporter of Joe Biden  the political climate here right now is  tense with the midterm elections just  over a week away the nation is bitterly  dangerously divided and those false  claims of a stolen election well they  linger and they agitate we don't yet  know precisely what the motive was for  this attack but the fact remains it is  the second time in two years that  speaker Pelosi has been the target  finish the proceeding on January the 6th  last year she was evacuated from our  office on Capitol Hill moments before a  mob arrived  the focus for investigators now is the  suspect's online footprint and links if  any to known extremist groups Mark Stone  Sky News in Washington
 

